
00:01:09.686 --> 00:01:14.557
I never really planned to be a life volunteer when I came to live in North Sea.

00:01:14.557 --> 00:01:19.977
I've been working in London as a website designer, but although that was interesting.

00:01:19.977 --> 00:01:22.201
I didn't like city life.

00:01:22.201 --> 00:01:32.188
I've been really keen on boats as a teenager and I thought if I went to live by the sea I might be able to pursue that interest a bit more in my free time.

00:01:32.188 --> 00:01:39.165
Then I found that the Lifeboat Institution was looking for volunteers, so I decided to apply.

00:01:39.165 --> 00:01:44.136
The Lifeboat Institution building here in North Sea is hard to miss.

00:01:44.136 --> 00:01:46.884
It's one of the largest in the country.

00:01:46.884 --> 00:01:53.992
It was built 15 years ago, with funds provided by a generous member of the public who'd lived here all her life.

00:01:53.992 --> 00:02:01.405
As the Lifeboat Institution is a charity that relies on that kind of donation, rather than funding provided by the government.

00:02:01.405 --> 00:02:03.804
That was a huge help to us.

00:02:03.804 --> 00:02:07.467
When I applied, I had to have a health assessment.

00:02:07.467 --> 00:02:11.304
The doctors were particularly interested in my vision.

00:02:11.304 --> 00:02:19.939
I used to be short-sighted, so I'd had to wear glasses, but I'd had laser eye surgery two years earlier, so that was okay.

00:02:19.939 --> 00:02:27.919
They gave me tests for colour blindness, and they thought I might have a problem there, but it turned out I was okay.

00:02:27.919 --> 00:02:34.846
When the Coast Guard gets an alert, all the volunteers are contacted and rushed to the lifeboat station.

00:02:34.846 --> 00:02:38.036
Our targets to get there in five minutes.

00:02:38.036 --> 00:02:44.621
Then we try to get the boat off the dock and out to sea in another six to eight minutes.

00:02:44.621 --> 00:02:47.805
Our team's proud that we usually achieve that.

00:02:47.805 --> 00:02:52.558
The average time across the country is eight and a half minutes.

00:02:52.633 --> 00:03:00.669
I've recently qualified as what's called a helmsman, which means I have the ultimate responsibility for the lifeboat.

00:03:00.669 --> 00:03:04.420
I have to check that the equipment we use is in working order.

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:14.696
The crew have special life jackets that can support up to four people in the water, and it's ultimately my decision whether it's safe to launch the boat.

00:03:14.696 --> 00:03:19.454
But it's very rare not to launch it, even in the worst weather.

00:03:19.454 --> 00:03:24.479
As well as going out on the lifeboat, my work involves other things too.

00:03:24.479 --> 00:03:39.612
A lot of people underestimate how quickly conditions can change at sea, so I speak to youth groups and sailing clubs in the area about the sorts of problems that sailors and swimmers can have if the weather suddenly gets bad.

00:03:39.612 --> 00:03:47.840
We also have a lot of volunteers who organise activities to raise money for us, and we couldn't manage without them.

00:04:24.703 --> 00:04:33.119
The training we get is a continuous process, focusing on technical competence and safe handling techniques.

00:04:33.119 --> 00:04:38.788
And it's given me the confidence to deal with extreme situations without panicking.

00:04:38.788 --> 00:04:46.982
I was glad I'd done a first aid course before I started, as that's a big help with the casualty care activities we do.

00:04:46.982 --> 00:04:53.526
We've done a lot on how to deal with ropes and tie knots, that's an essential skill.

00:04:53.789 --> 00:04:59.378
After a year, I did a one week residential course, led by specialists.

00:04:59.378 --> 00:05:10.981
They had a wave tank, where they could create extreme weather conditions so we could get experience at what to do if the boat turned over in a storm at night for example.

00:05:10.981 --> 00:05:19.221
Since I started I've had to deal with a range of emergency situations but the works hugely motivating.

00:05:19.221 --> 00:05:22.296
It's not just about saving lives.

00:05:22.296 --> 00:05:25.296
I've learned a lot about the technology involved.

00:05:25.296 --> 00:05:32.546
My background in IT has been useful here and I can use my expertise to help other volunteers.

00:05:32.546 --> 00:05:34.138
They're a great group.

00:05:34.171 --> 00:05:41.081
We're like a family really which helps when you're dragging yourself out of bed on a cold stormy night.

00:05:41.081 --> 00:05:46.207
But actually, it's the colder months that can be the most rewarding time.

00:05:46.207 --> 00:05:53.611
That's when the incidents tend to be more serious and you realize that you can make a huge difference to the outcome.

00:05:53.611 --> 00:05:59.202
So if any of you listeners are interested why don't you give us a call.
